 ### A run
 
-1. Ride within 12 tiles of a train (`commit.rangeTiles`, measured to the nearest car). A flashing "Commit to this train?" banner appears and that train is outlined pale blue. Press E to commit, wait out the bar (`commit.timerSec`, 2 s), or ride within 4 tiles (`commit.closeRangeTiles`). Ride away before then to just look. Once committed the run is in `approach`, the train is yours, and health is full.
+1. Ride within 12 tiles of a train (`commit.rangeTiles`, measured to the nearest car). A flashing "Commit to this train?" banner appears and that train is outlined pale blue. Press E to commit, wait out the bar (`commit.timerSec`, 2 s), or ride within 4 tiles (`commit.closeRangeTiles`). Ride away before then to just look. Once committed the run is in `approach` and the train is yours. Health is not refilled: it lasts the whole day (see `health.scope`).
 2. Ride beside a door on either side. The **boarding** line comes from the sim's own rule: `ELIGIBLE` (in range and speed matched), `TOO FAST`, `TOO SLOW` or `TOO FAR`, the side you are on, the distance to the nearest door on that side, and your speed along the car minus the train's.
 3. In range, the meter above the horse sweeps back and forth: slowly with a white marker when your speed matches the train's, fast with an orange marker when it doesn't. Out of range it is dim and parked. The green band is perfect, the yellow band around it is good, the rest fails. The bands move to a new random place after every jump, never while you are lining up.
-4. Space jumps. Out of range it is refused (`TOO FAR`); at the wrong speed it is allowed, just on the faster meter. A **perfect** landing puts you in the car; a **good** one too, with a 1.5 s stumble at a third of walking speed; a **fail** throws you clear, stuns the horse for 1.5 s at half its speed (it ignores the reins), costs 15 health under `time-and-damage`, and the train pulls ahead. Seven failures from full health kill you: "YOU DIED", and you are back at the spawn.
+4. Space jumps. Out of range it is refused (`TOO FAR`); at the wrong speed it is allowed, just on the faster meter. A **perfect** landing puts you in the car; a **good** one too, with a 1.5 s stumble at a third of walking speed; a **fail** throws you clear, stuns the horse for 1.5 s at half its speed (it ignores the reins), costs 15 health under `time-and-damage`, and the train pulls ahead. Seven failures from full health kill you: you are back at the spawn and a new day starts at full health.
 5. Aboard, walk the car with WASD (Shift runs, C crouches). Out of an end door is the platform (walk only) and the coupling plate to the next car; out of a side door is the narrow ledge along the car, slow but out of sight except through windows and doors. On an end platform a ladder (E) takes you up to the roof: slower going, unseen by guards inside, but the guard in the car below can hear you and will climb up to check. Space jumps the gap to the next roof, and running on a curve can make you slip (push the other way to lean into it). A good landing staggers you two tiles into the car, loudly; a perfect one leaves you in the doorway. The view keeps the train's direction on screen. Esc or R ends the run.
 6. If a guard catches you, you're thrown back onto your horse with part of your loot, and the train shuts its doors: its side doors turn to dark barred planks and you can't jump back on. Press F to get away and bank what you carry, or Tab to another train in range. Esc ends the run without banking anything.
 
 When the clock hits 0 while your horse is alongside and you stand at a door on its side, you get 3 s more (`countdown.graceSec`) to jump. "OUT OF TIME: jump now!" with the seconds left shows just above the mount meter. In the last 10 s with the horse alongside, the panel reminds you that a door gives you that extra time.
 
